# Every image builds from the repo root (compose uses `context: ..`), so this one
# file governs all of them.

# Dependencies are installed *inside* the image. Letting the host's copies in is
# not just slower: `COPY gateway gateway` runs after `npm install` and would
# overwrite the container's Linux node_modules with Windows-built ones. That only
# happens to work while every dependency is pure JavaScript.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Secrets reach containers through compose's env_file at runtime, never through
# the image. Excluding them here means a future careless `COPY . .` cannot bake a
# key into a layer that outlives the key.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime data, not source. storage/ holds users' uploaded recordings and images.
storage
models
*.pth
*.onnx
*.bin

# Not part of any image.
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
legacy
*.log
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
